# Testing

Backend tests should be split into:

- use-case tests with an in-memory class that implements the same port interface
- repository integration tests against the real PostgreSQL test database
- HTTP integration tests through the application

Do not mock the database for repository or HTTP integration tests. Compose currently runs one development database. Do not point tests at it. Add a separate test database before repository integration tests.

The first persistence feature must include a test where two repositories share one transaction and rollback undoes both writes.

Frontend behavior that is worth locking in should use Vitest and React Testing Library when those tests are added.

End-to-end coverage uses Playwright. Playwright is not a substitute for use-case or repository tests.

Do not treat a green test suite as proof that architecture boundaries were respected. Run lint, typecheck, and dependency-cruiser as well.

`@erp/test-utils` is for shared test helpers. Do not put product assertions or business fixtures there until a real shared need exists.
